<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Ceval 1996 net $30.1 million.</title>
<headline>Brazil Ceval 1996 net $30.1 million.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian food processor</p>
<p>Ceval issued the following statement on its 1996 results.</p>
<p>		     1996			1995</p>
<p>    shr		$0.86		     N/A</p>
<p>    net		$30.1 million		 N/A</p>
<p>    rvs		$2.69 bln		    N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: All data provided in U.S. dollars. Share profit figures provided per 1,000 shares.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement its net profit in the second half of 1996 overshadowed the $12.3 million loss posted in the first half of the year.</p>
<p>Last year, Ceval's revenues rose four percent over 1995 while its exports reached $1.3 billion, an increase of 11.9 percent.</p>
<p>Domestic sales totalled $1.39 billion last year, a drop of 2.7 percent over 1995, it added.</p>
<p>It said its gross operating margins last year fell 11.3 percent over 1995 due to an increase in raw material prices.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
